      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-19934",
      ":question/problem": "A particle $P$ moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$. Its velocity $vm/s$ is given by $v(t) =-t^{2} + 8t - 7$, where $t$ is the time in seconds. Calculate the total distance traveled by $P$ in the interval $2 \\le t \\le 6$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
